{
  "_doc": "Kits and cultures of the modern, contemporary, futuristic and alien styles. Same schema as styles.json (kits, derive, cultures: {<culture id>: {kit, traits}}); merged after it by forms/kit.rs. Every culture here states traits.era (modern | futuristic | alien): the singular buildings of parcels/monuments/modern.rs and metropolis.rs serve the cultures that have one, and the web reads it (gen/options.ts cultureEra). traits.roleGroups names the override groups of roles_modern.json the culture shares, after its own overrides. palettes.<id> = {homes, special}: weighted wall tints (sRGB \"#rrggbb\": weight); traits.palette names the culture's palette. massing.rs draws one tint per building from the building's seed (special: landmarks, non-dwelling lots and dwellings of 9 storeys or more; homes otherwise) and writes it as the piece's `tint`; a culture without a palette emits none. ladders.<id> = [[population, storeys]…] (ascending): the height ladder named by traits.heightLadder caps the storeys of a style's ordinary buildings by the settlement's population (forms/kit.rs storey_cap, read by massing.rs and the programme's household capacity), so a modern town of 10 000 stays low and towers come from about 50 000; a quarter the user sets as city core (layout overrides.quarters.<i>.zone = \"core\") takes the top step. The tall singular buildings (housing.tower, housing.slab, office blocks, skyscrapers, megastructures, arcologies, tv towers) come by population through their minPop in services.json. traits.suburbRing (bool): the outermost growth epoch of a town of two epochs or more is built with the culture's faubourg tissue in the edge zone (footprint.rs epoch_zone): a dense core, a mid-density ring, then a ring of detached houses on small lots; a style that densifies (an arcology, habitat domes) leaves it off and keeps its compact rings. Materials of the modern styles: walls concrete, glass, steel, ashlar (cut limestone) besides the historical ones; covers zinc, bitumen (flat roofs), glass.",
